  "worked_solution": "From the phase line, we can deduce the following:\n\n- The equilibrium solutions are $y=0$ and $y=3.$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along these lines.\n\n- $f(y)<0$ for $y\\in (-\\infty ,0).$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are negative in this region.\n\n- $f(y)>0$ for $y\\in (0,3)\\cup (3,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are positive in these regions.\n\nThe only slope field that satisfies the above conditions is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14094575/assets/1b31ffbacee1f8910daa6a57094060dee4401589903724ab73cf7d99ffa85ba4.png)",
